@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Category reports
+
+Many households already filter at the DNS level, for example with a family DNS service or a Pi-hole. **Categories** shows how much of each kind of site that filter already blocks, so you can see where FamilyFi's own rules are still needed.
+
+**These are reports only.** A category report never blocks or unblocks anything, and FamilyFi never creates a gateway policy from one. To block a category, make a [rule](Rules-schedules-pause-and-allow).
+
+![The Categories page](images/categories.png)
+
+## How it works
+
+Each category (AI, Adult, Dating, Gambling, Gaming and more) is a list of test websites. FamilyFi looks each one up through your DNS and records whether it came back blocked:
+
+| Result | Means |
+| --- | --- |
+| **Blocked upstream** | Your DNS blocked every test website in the category. |
+| **Partially blocked** | It blocked some of them. |
+| **Not blocked** | It blocked none of them. |
+| **Not checked** | FamilyFi hasn't checked yet, or couldn't. It never means *not blocked*. |
+
+The same results appear on each person's card and page, next to the categories FamilyFi's own rules cover.
+
+## Choosing the DNS to check
+
+By default, FamilyFi checks through the DNS servers your UniFi gateway hands out. If your filter is a DNS-over-HTTPS service, select **Add DoH override** under **DNS resolver** and paste its address, for example `https://dns.example.com/dns-query/profile`. **Remove** goes back to your gateway's DNS servers.
+
+Checks run from the FamilyFi computer. A device on another network may get a different answer if that network hands out different DNS servers; open a category to see **Results by network**.
+
+## When it checks
+
+Under **Check schedule**, pick the days and the **Check time**. **Check all now** checks every category straight away, and **Check now** on a category's page checks just that one. Turning checking **Off** clears earlier results; **Check now** still works.
+
+## Your own categories
+
+**New category** adds a list of your own. Open any category to see its test websites, **Add a domain**, or **Remove** one. The built-in lists are kept up to date with each FamilyFi release.
